Given the standard entry point of a modern Symfony 8 application running with Symfony Flex:<br><br><code>// public/index.php<br>use App\Kernel;<br><br>require_once dirname(__DIR__).'/vendor/autoload_runtime.php';<br><br>return static function (array $context) {<br>    return new Kernel($context['APP_ENV'], (bool) $context['APP_DEBUG']);<br>};</code><br><br>Where are the standard lifecycle methods <code>$kernel->handle($request)->send();</code> executed, since they are no longer visible in public/index.php?	They are executed internally by the <b>Symfony Runtime Component</b> inside <b><code>vendor/autoload_runtime.php</code></b>. The application bootstrap returns a closure, which is intercepted by the configuration runner (e.g., <code>SymfonyRuntime</code>) that automatically manages Request creation, Kernel handling, and sending the Response back to the server buffer.
Look at this controller snippet attempting to read a raw JSON payload from an incoming POST request:<br><br><code>namespace App\Controller;<br>use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request;<br>use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;<br><br>class ApiController {<br>    public function handle(Request $request): Response {<br>        // Line to fetch raw body content<br>        $content = $request->getContent();<br>    }<br>}</code><br><br>True or False: If you call <code>$request->getContent(true)</code> (passing true as the first argument), Symfony will return a PHP resource stream instead of a string, which is highly optimized for memory when handling large JSON payloads.	<b>True.</b> Passing true to <code>$request->getContent()</code> returns a <b>PHP resource pointer (stream)</b> instead of loading the entire payload into a PHP string variable, which complies with memory-efficiency standards for large payloads.
During a Symfony Flex recipe installation, a bundle requires configuration injection into <code>config/packages/</code>. What is the exact name and format of the file that a custom Flex recipe uses internally to define these automated framework configurations and file-copy tasks?	The <b><code>manifest.json</code></b> file, which resides within the specific Flex recipe repository structure to map targets, configuration files, and environment variable defaults.
